  "overview": {
    "claims": [
      {
        "attribution": "Eric Schnaufer",
        "citations": [
          {
            "document_hash": "9d1ddb689fb1bc2a11f54196b6f57eb0975a9b2ad671d32908106ff3241aa043",
            "evidence_ids": [
              "ev-9d1ddb689fb1-0000-0001"
            ],
            "pages": {
              "end": 3,
              "start": 3
            }
          }
        ],
        "text": "Eric Schnaufer argued that 42\u202fU.S.C.\u202f\u00a7\u202f406(b) requires attorney fees to be contingent on success and that district\u2011court fee awards should reflect that contingent nature."
      },
      {
        "attribution": "Eric Schnaufer",
        "citations": [
          {
            "document_hash": "9d1ddb689fb1bc2a11f54196b6f57eb0975a9b2ad671d32908106ff3241aa043",
            "evidence_ids": [
              "ev-9d1ddb689fb1-0000-0003"
            ],
            "pages": {
              "end": 8,
              "start": 8
            }
          }
        ],
        "text": "Eric Schnaufer contended that district courts awarded non\u2011contingent hourly rates, which he said is contrary to the statutory requirement that fees be contingent."
      },
      {
        "attribution": "Government",
        "citations": [
          {
            "document_hash": "9d1ddb689fb1bc2a11f54196b6f57eb0975a9b2ad671d32908106ff3241aa043",
            "evidence_ids": [
              "ev-9d1ddb689fb1-0002-0005"
            ],
            "pages": {
              "end": 38,
              "start": 38
            }
          }
        ],
        "text": "The Government says the statute directs courts to determine a reasonable fee."
      },
      {
        "attribution": "Government",
        "citations": [
          {
            "document_hash": "9d1ddb689fb1bc2a11f54196b6f57eb0975a9b2ad671d32908106ff3241aa043",
            "evidence_ids": [
              "ev-9d1ddb689fb1-0002-0003"
            ],
            "pages": {
              "end": 37,
              "start": 37
            }
          }
        ],
        "text": "According to Government, the Government states that the Commissioner interprets \u00a7\u202f406(b) to require only contingent fees."
      },
      {
        "attribution": "Government",
        "citations": [
          {
            "document_hash": "9d1ddb689fb1bc2a11f54196b6f57eb0975a9b2ad671d32908106ff3241aa043",
            "evidence_ids": [
              "ev-9d1ddb689fb1-0002-0007"
            ],
            "pages": {
              "end": 40,
              "start": 40
            }
          }
        ],
        "text": "The Government says Congress enacted the statute to address a market failure in which lawyers charged excessively large contingency fees in Social Security cases."
      },
      {
        "attribution": "Government",
        "citations": [
          {
            "document_hash": "9d1ddb689fb1bc2a11f54196b6f57eb0975a9b2ad671d32908106ff3241aa043",
            "evidence_ids": [
              "ev-9d1ddb689fb1-0002-0010"
            ],
            "pages": {
              "end": 42,
              "start": 42
            }
          }
        ],
        "text": "According to Government, the Government notes that the agency rarely appeals attorney\u2011fee awards unless the case raises a broader legal principle."
      },
      {
        "attribution": "Government",
        "citations": [
          {
            "document_hash": "9d1ddb689fb1bc2a11f54196b6f57eb0975a9b2ad671d32908106ff3241aa043",
            "evidence_ids": [
              "ev-9d1ddb689fb1-0002-0018"
            ],
            "pages": {
              "end": 49,
              "start": 49
            }
          }
        ],
        "text": "The Government argues that the lodestar method has been used for decades in six circuits without evidence that it harms counsel availability."
      }
    ],
